      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:2:34:7",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنْ رَجُلٍ طَلَّقَ امْرَأَتَهُ بَعْدَ مَا وَلَدَتْ وَ طَهُرَتْ وَ هِيَ امْرَأَةٌ لَا تَرَى دَماً مَا دَامَتْ تُرْضِعُ مَا عِدَّتُهَا قَالَ ثَلَاثَةُ أَشْهُرٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Nasr, from Dawood Bin Al Husayn, from Abu Al Abbas who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about a man who divorced his wife after having given birth, and purified, and she is a woman who does not see blood for as long as she breast-feeds. What is her waiting period?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Three months’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "7. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu Nasr, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from abu al-‘Abbas who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the case of a man who divorces his wife after childbirth and her becoming clean and she is a woman who does not experience Hayd (menses) as long as she breastfeeds and about how much is her waiting period. He (the Imam) said, ‘It is three months.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
